### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 1: Login first to get a token
### (user-service on 8081)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@devflow.com",
  "password": "securepass123"
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 2: Create a product
### Paste token from STEP 1 into Authorization
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
POST http://localhost:8082/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Email: john@devflow.com

{
  "name": "DevFlow API Toolkit",
  "description": "A complete toolkit for building REST APIs",
  "price": 49.99,
  "category": "API_TOOL"
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 3: Get all products
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 4: Get product by ID
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/1

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 5: Place an order
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Email: john@devflow.com

{
  "productId": 1
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 6: Get my orders
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
GET http://localhost:8082/api/orders
X-User-Email: john@devflow.com

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 7: GraphQL - get all products
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
POST http://localhost:8082/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "{ products { id name price category } }"
}

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
### STEP 8: GraphQL - get specific fields only
### Notice we ask for LESS fields than REST returns
### This is the power of GraphQL
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
POST http://localhost:8082/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "{ product(id: 1) { name price } }"
}